 given the concerns that the  police had  uh from what they had seen in previous  attacks that it did amount to a breach  of his conditions and he should have  been recalled to prison so a missed  opportunity there by the probation  service the two other questions they  were asked to consider really were  centered around the actions of the  police one was whether the police should  have searched the room he was staying at  he was staying  at a probation hostel not far from  streatham high road after his release  from prison in the days before the  attack  the jury though concluded though  that in terms of searching  that probation hostel  that the police did the right thing in  not doing that that it would have been  difficult for them to do it  to try to  organize for members of staff in that  hostel to carry out  a search a delicate search of this young  man's room at times when he wasn't there  and he was there  an awful lot in the days before the  attack he hardly left his room  and the third uh  question that they were asked to  consider was really around this young  man when he left on the morning of the  attack of the afternoon of the attack it  was 22 minutes past one in the afternoon  that he left the hostel  to go to stratham high road at that  point  they were asked should the police have  stopped and searched him because of his  behavior he was walking quite slowly at  times he doubled back on himself at  times but the jury again felt that the  police actions in just following him  quite closely there were nine  surveillance officers some of those  officers were armed  some were in cars one was on a motorbike  others were on foot  because of his actions  they believed that the police were  actually justified in just continuing to  follow him rather than stopping him so  really i think as far as the police  handling of the surveillance operation  surrounding sudetshaman and the response  to him launching the attack that day  they have been cleared by the 